<slide xmlns="https://www.larkoffice.com/sml/2.0">
  <data>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="10" width="400" height="20">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(39,121,167,1)" wrap="false" textAlign="left">
        <p>STOP 9 / 11 - PARSE THE BANK RESPONSE</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="30" width="848" height="34">
      <content textType="title" fontSize="24" fontFamily="Inter" bold="true" color="rgba(15,36,64,1)" wrap="false" textAlign="left">
        <p>Parse: read the bank's answer exactly once</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <line startX="56" startY="64" endX="904" endY="64">
      <border color="rgb(39, 121, 167)" width="2"/>
    </line>
    <shape type="rect" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="84" width="532" height="384">
      <fill>
        <fillColor color="rgba(247,249,251,1)"/>
      </fill>
      <border color="rgb(214, 222, 232)" width="1"/>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="72" topLeftY="100" width="504" height="352">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="11" fontFamily="Roboto Mono" color="rgba(61,74,92,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.32" textAlign="left">
        <p>BankResponse bankResponse = objectMapper</p>
        <p>    .readValue(ctx.getBankResponse(),</p>
        <p>               BankResponse.class);</p>
        <p>PaymentStatus status = PaymentStatus</p>
        <p>    .fromAuthorized(bankResponse.isAuthorized());</p>
        <p>context.setPaymentStatus(status);</p>
        <p>context.setAuthorizationCode(</p>
        <p>    normalize(bankResponse.getAuthCode()));</p>
        <p>// one class owns the bank DTO -</p>
        <p>// no other node imports it</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="604" topLeftY="92" width="300" height="250">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="13.5" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(61,74,92,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.4" textAlign="left">
        <ul>
          <li><p>One place reads the bank DTO - a single mapping table, a single import.</p></li>
          <li><p>isAuthorized() becomes the domain enum once; the auth code is normalized here.</p></li>
          <li><p>Flat fields on the context decouple the later nodes from the bank's JSON shape.</p></li>
          <li><p>Pattern: the Adapter sits at the boundary.</p></li>
        </ul>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="rect" topLeftX="604" topLeftY="360" width="300" height="108">
      <fill>
        <fillColor color="rgba(232,241,247,1)"/>
      </fill>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="616" topLeftY="374" width="276" height="84">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="13" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(15,36,64,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.35" textAlign="left">
        <p>Why it matters: if the bank renames a field tomorrow, exactly one class knows about it.</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="856" topLeftY="510" width="48" height="18">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(138,148,166,1)" textAlign="right" wrap="false">
        <p>15 / 24</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
  </data>
  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>Stop nine converts the bank's raw JSON into domain meaning, and it is the only place that does. The response is deserialized into a bank DTO that lives in the client package, isAuthorized is mapped to our status enum once, and the auth code is normalized. Everything the later nodes need is then put on the context as plain fields - so the rest of the code never sees the bank's JSON shape. If the bank renames a field, exactly one class changes.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
</slide>
